  "headword": "{領海|りょうかい}",
  "reading": "りょうかい",
  "part_of_speech": "noun",
  "gloss": "territorial waters; territorial sea",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "territorial waters; territorial sea",
      "explanation": "The area of sea adjacent to a country's coast over which it exercises sovereignty. Under international law, this extends up to 12 nautical miles from the baseline."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "15850_ryoukai_ex1",
      "japanese": "{領海|りょうかい}に{侵入|しんにゅう}した。",
      "english": "They entered the territorial waters.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "15850_ryoukai_ex2",
      "japanese": "{外国|がいこく}の{船|ふね}が{領海|りょうかい}を{通過|つうか}した。",
      "english": "A foreign ship passed through the territorial waters.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "15850_ryoukai_ex3",
      "japanese": "{日本|にほん}の{領海|りょうかい}は{海岸線|かいがんせん}から12{海里|かいり}までと{定|さだ}められている。",
      "english": "Japan's territorial waters are defined as extending 12 nautical miles from the coastline.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{領|りょう} (territory) + {海|かい} (sea).\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n{領空|りょうくう} — territorial airspace\n{領土|りょうど} — territory (land)\n{排他的経済水域|はいたてきけいざいすいいき} (EEZ) — exclusive economic zone\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {領海|りょうかい}{侵犯|しんぱん} (violation of territorial waters)\n- {領海|りょうかい}に{侵入|しんにゅう}する (to intrude into territorial waters)\n- {領海|りょうかい}を{守|まも}る (to defend territorial waters)",
